{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview","id":1147432,"title":"Storypath System Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-06T08:22:14-07:00","id":1147432,"title":"Storypath System Preview","content":"The newest update for the Scion Kickstarter is out and it provides us with a look at the Storypath system! What are people\u2019s impressions of the system as it is right now?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rS_VsgfM6ycrRhhvCHq5XXf-TH5vPsgrxBojSlhTobk/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rS_VsgfM6ycrRhhvCHq5XXf-TH5vPsgrxBojSlhTobk/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rS_VsgfM6ycrRhhvCHq5XXf-TH5vPsgrxBojSlhTobk/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rS_VsgfM6ycrRhhvCHq5XXf-TH5vPsgrxBojSlhTobk/mobilebasic </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T08:54:46-07:00","id":1147451,"title":"","content":"Overall i like it. The group momentum thing seems fun and helps with the cohesion of the group.<br /> But i have to say, i'm more the type to understand the rules by using them. I'm having a bit of a difficulty fully grasping the rules just reading them.<br /> <br /> I would be curious to know which part is from the trinity breakthrough, but thats really just out of curiosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T10:25:40-07:00","id":1147481,"title":"","content":"So the attribute cap is now going to be 3 with 4 and 5 dots reserved for favored approach linked attributes you put 2 or 3 in before picking it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T11:33:54-07:00","id":1147502,"title":"","content":"I like the look of it. Some nice clear guidelines for the different systems, and it looks pretty flexible overall. Time will tell though, especially once we see the rest of the bells and whistles. It seems kind of easy to stat enhancements up to that +3 limit though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T11:47:29-07:00","id":1147508,"title":"","content":"Minor hiccup: Academics describes your languages known as Academics+Reason, but I don\u2019t see Reason anywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:07:16-07:00","id":1147517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147508#post1147508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor hiccup: Academics describes your languages known as Academics+Reason, but I don\u2019t see Reason anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Reason was the previous version of Intellect, the Mental Force Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:13:16-07:00","id":1147522,"title":"","content":"Ok, so am I interpreting this correctly and instead of individually placing dots into our Attributes, our stats our determined by our rank in each Arena and our Favored Approach?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I like that. If I want to make the dumb bruiser character, I\u2019m going to choose Force as my favored approach, which means I\u2019m getting a boost to Strength (yay!) and Intellect (boo!). Why? What if I want to make a character who is charming and composed in social situations but who is honest and straightforward to a fault? Is there a way to have a high Presence and Composure with a low Manipulation? How does this system work with character advancement? Will we even be able to increase our starting Attributes at all? <br /> <br /> No, unless we get some clarification on this system, I have to say I\u2019m not a fan. You\u2019re removing a lot of freedom and fine control from the players in making the character they want to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:16:03-07:00","id":1147524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147522#post1147522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so am I interpreting this correctly and instead of individually placing dots into our Attributes, our stats our determined by our rank in each Arena and our Favored Approach?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I like that. If I want to make the dumb bruiser character, I\u2019m going to choose Force as my favored approach, which means I\u2019m getting a boost to Strength (yay!) and Intellect (boo!). Why? What if I want to make a character who is charming and composed in social situations but who is honest and straightforward to a fault? Is there a way to have a high Presence and Composure with a low Manipulation? How does this system work with character advancement? Will we even be able to increase our starting Attributes at all?<br /> <br /> No, unless we get some clarification on this system, I have to say I\u2019m not a fan. You\u2019re removing a lot of freedom and fine control from the players in making the character they want to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's somewhat unclear since the Advancement rules given with the Netjer Preview had you buying your Attributes up with EXP rather than Arenas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:17:38-07:00","id":1147526,"title":"","content":"We got an advancement cost table in the July preview. So yeah you'll be able to increase them just fine, but your concern about choosing Force mandating being pretty smart is one I never even thought till just now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:17:52-07:00","id":1147527,"title":"","content":"I'm at work right now and can't post a lot, but for now I have to say at first reading I am deeply confused and concerned by the function of Skill Specialties .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:25:04-07:00","id":1147530,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s interesting that Attributes cap out at 3 and skills cap out at 5, but I guess could be justified in that it\u2019s easier to learn a skill than change a fundamental aspect of yourself. I do find it odd though that Demigods and Gods have the same target number when Gods should have an easier time making their influence known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:28:30-07:00","id":1147532,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it's that bad. We haven't seen character creation and how Arena assignments work for PCs. The Arena/Approach simplification makes stating up NPCs a ton faster for when you're not worried about as much fine detail as players will want.<br /> <br /> There's also Conditions to add back in some fine control for players. Manipulation isn't just the &quot;being dishonest&quot; trait. It's the Social Finesse trait. It's how well you use subtlety and tact, as well as playing with words. &quot;Honest to a Fault&quot; can be a Condition that gives you penalties on lying. That way you can have a decent Manipulation for truthful statements that need to be massaged into the conversation, but suck at actually lying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:39:09-07:00","id":1147535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147530#post1147530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s interesting that Attributes cap out at 3 and skills cap out at 5, but I guess could be justified in that it\u2019s easier to learn a skill than change a fundamental aspect of yourself. I do find it odd though that Demigods and Gods have the same target number when Gods should have an easier time making their influence known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite - Arenas cap at 3. Attributes, which are a composite of your Arena and your Approach, cap at 5 (3 from the Arena, +2 for Favored Approach).<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not 100% sold on the Arena+Approach=Attribute bit. It's nice for a quick character, but I do feel like you lose some granularity like mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:51:35-07:00","id":1147538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147527#post1147527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm at work right now and can't post a lot, but for now I have to say at first reading I am deeply confused and concerned by the function of Skill Specialties .</div> </div> </div> </div>If you fail in a roll in which you've got a specialty, you get extra Momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T12:56:50-07:00","id":1147541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeldafan42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147522#post1147522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so am I interpreting this correctly and instead of individually placing dots into our Attributes, our stats our determined by our rank in each Arena and our Favored Approach?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if I like that. If I want to make the dumb bruiser character, I\u2019m going to choose Force as my favored approach, which means I\u2019m getting a boost to Strength (yay!) and Intellect (boo!). Why? What if I want to make a character who is charming and composed in social situations but who is honest and straightforward to a fault? Is there a way to have a high Presence and Composure with a low Manipulation? How does this system work with character advancement? Will we even be able to increase our starting Attributes at all?<br /> <br /> No, unless we get some clarification on this system, I have to say I\u2019m not a fan. You\u2019re removing a lot of freedom and fine control from the players in making the character they want to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang, I completely overlooked that bit about arenas. That's a house rule if you're right. I kind of like the favored approach thing though. It's not perfect but I can see what the intent of it was, a direct person will probably be direct in all areas of their life, If you have the willpower to have a high resolve you'll likely be able to keep your cool with composure and push through pain with stamina. So it's more a personality indicator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T13:13:11-07:00","id":1147552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147538#post1147538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you fail in a roll in which you've got a specialty, you get extra Momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't the part I was confused over. <br /> <br /> Coming at this as a long time ST system fan, it seems deeply counterintuitive to make your Specialties (which have historically made you more likely to succeed) of no real benefit to you unless you fail at them.<br /> <br /> Trying to step back, though, I'm going to hazard a guess: a specialty in Storypath isn't a mode you're good at but a distant relative of the attributes' favored approach, encouraging players to take a certain tack under the rationale that if they fail they'll still get some sort of benefit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T13:18:14-07:00","id":1147556,"title":"","content":"I just double checked the character creation preview and it does seem like character advancement allows you to buy individual dots in Attributes, so it seems that the weirdness of the Arena+Approach system mostly is just a character creation thing. <br /> <br /> Honestly, Favored Approach doesn\u2019t bother me as much outside of Strength and Intellect being tied to the same approach. That just feels weird that the obvious character creation choice for building the dumb bruiser archetype somehow makes you smarter.<br /> <br /> No, I think it\u2019s this Arena thing that bothers me. It sounds like it\u2019s great for quick character creation and perfect for generating fast NPCs, but...until I see exactly how it effects character creation it feels like it\u2019s removing a lot of fine tuning from character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T13:31:15-07:00","id":1147562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147552#post1147552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wasn't the part I was confused over.<br /> <br /> Coming at this as a long time ST system fan, it seems deeply counterintuitive to make your Specialties (which have historically made you more likely to succeed) of no real benefit to you unless you fail at them.<br /> <br /> Trying to step back, though, I'm going to hazard a guess: a specialty in Storypath isn't a mode you're good at but a distant relative of the attributes' favored approach, encouraging players to take a certain tack under the rationale that if they fail they'll still get some sort of benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this for the most part. But I imagine it's from the narrative perspective. The person that\u2019s an expert at X fails at a difficult task only to eventually succeed once they have enough momentum. And the slight weirdness is a result of it becoming a group pool (which still makes sense from a purely narrative sense).<br /> <br /> Side note: Am I the only one that finds it odd that good liars are automatically good lockpicks and fences?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T13:38:44-07:00","id":1147568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147562#post1147562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Side note: Am I the only one that finds it odd that good liars are automatically good lockpicks and fences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the game is going for narrative genre emulation rather than realism, that seems appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-06-2017, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T13:44:47-07:00","id":1147570,"title":"","content":"There's an optional rule in the SG chapter (one of many optional rules) that allows you to condense the Focus down to one Attribute if that's what you prefer - and yes, there are Conditions that come into play to emulate strong-but-stupid folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T14:28:10-07:00","id":1147584,"title":"","content":"Re: Arenas being weird for fine tuning.<br /> <br /> Considering you begin with 15 XP at character creation, I think you're expected to customize your Attributes by purchasing dots after determining the initial values of your Arenas, if you want to. Are those correct expectations, Neall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T14:32:20-07:00","id":1147585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147570#post1147570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an optional rule in the SG chapter (one of many optional rules) that allows you to condense the Focus down to one Attribute if that's what you prefer - and yes, there are Conditions that come into play to emulate strong-but-stupid folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the main rules have three traits by arena as we're used to, to try and get this perfectly understood in the thread if so? Just to head off future arguments or misconceptions on this one front","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T18:06:05-07:00","id":1147626,"title":"","content":"Good that you can focus on a single Attribute and that are mechanisms to achieve stuff such as &quot;strong-but-dumb&quot;. I really like the idea of favored approaches, but that sort of conflation &quot;strong = smart&quot; really soured me on the Cypher system right off the bat (though in that case it was &quot;smart = socially capable&quot; that ticked me off if I'm not mistaken)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T21:23:23-07:00","id":1147660,"title":"","content":"Something else these are the base human rules we don\u2019t know what might be changed when you add the Hero aspect from Hero","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6379-tytalan","name":"tytalan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T07:41:05-07:00","id":1147760,"title":"","content":"So, having taken a look... There's a lot I like. Some ideas I'll want to try out before I make a final call, but there's a lot where at the least I like the IDEA behind them.<br /> <br /> Also: Bonds. Banked successes that can help your friend that can be recharged by role-playing a night on the town that may or may not end with laughing in a jail cell and admitting that hey, at least it was awesome.<br /> <br /> I feel that the phrase &quot;All of my YES!&quot; is insufficient to encompass how much I love this idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T08:49:34-07:00","id":1147782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147760#post1147760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, having taken a look... There's a lot I like. Some ideas I'll want to try out before I make a final call, but there's a lot where at the least I like the IDEA behind them.<br /> <br /> Also: Bonds. Banked successes that can help your friend that can be recharged by role-playing a night on the town that may or may not end with laughing in a jail cell and admitting that hey, at least it was awesome.<br /> <br /> I feel that the phrase &quot;All of my YES!&quot; is insufficient to encompass how much I love this idea</div> </div> </div> </div>And suddenly everyone wants a scion of Dionysis on the band...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T09:54:36-07:00","id":1147803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147782#post1147782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And suddenly everyone wants a scion of Dionysis on the band...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Loki. Or half of the Tuatha. Or Sun Wukong. Or-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T10:35:56-07:00","id":1147813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147803#post1147803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Loki. Or half of the Tuatha. Or Sun Wukong. Or-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but listing every single god of good times would take all day :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T10:49:30-07:00","id":1147821,"title":"","content":"Just want to say i absolutely love the crafting rules, perfect in my opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T04:14:57-07:00","id":1148268,"title":"","content":"I haven't read all of the preview yet, but like a few others in this thread I was immediately soured by the idea of assigning points to arena's and boosting an approach, for the same reasons already mentioned. The idea of not being able to have, ie, the strong but dumb or the highly composed strong personality with no tact to speak of seemed very bothersome. With what has been said about there being options to represent those kinds of specific character faults, and after some more reflection, I think I'm basically ok with the idea now.<br /> <br /> It still feels weird, just from my 'gamer' perspective, not having more granularity in attribute selection, but the more I think about it it's not inappropriate for the subject of this particular game. Just off the top of my head you don't really get mythic heroes who are good at one or two parts of an arena but not the rest, like Hercules was known for his epic strength but his other physicals were certainly not low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T10:39:45-07:00","id":1148358,"title":"","content":"Okay, I clearly missed the fact that the 3 maximum on a attribute applied to player characters as well. Also, thinking back to it you also have the ability to spend 5xp to change your favored approach from the xp cost chart. I'm not going to lie, I dont see the benefit of a favored approach or arena as its being called here at all. I also absolutely hate mechanics that make people pay xp they will never get back simply to change their character which is likely intended for story purposes. It really hurts the player trying to make an organic character while promoting staying steadfast and unchanging. I've always encouraged the spend the xp temporary idea in those cases... spend 5 xp but gain it back 1 or 2 xp a session for free until you are back to the same xp total as everyone else.<br /> <br /> I really think this 3 cap on stats + favored approach needs to be scrapped... or atleast could you please give us some insight into why this is useful from a gameplay perspective? We don't need mechanics that feel like a quick creation tool. This game is designed for intelligent people who care to delve into the intricacies of mythology... we need options, not simplicity. Especially when defining our characters through their attributes and skills.<br /> <br /> Neall, Could you please give us some insight into why this system was chosen? As well as the benefits you have seen? Thank you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Personally, id rather see the 1-5 dots in attributes and 1-5 dots in skills like we are used to and we know works. Rereading it it sounds like we will have a certain number of points to simply divide among Physical Mental and Social and all attributes within those categories are set to the same number. 3 Physical for instance giving you 3 Might, Dex, and Stamina and then you simply getting a +2 in whichever approach you chose. So a force approach would then yield 5 Might, 3 Dex, and 3 Stamina.<br /> <br /> Is that all correct? Or is an approach simply +2 and you can still raise your attributes to 5 through advancement? To be honest, this is giving me ptsd flashbacks to how confusing the damage system was on the first try as well... and we still haven't been able to see how that looks now.<br /> <br /> Not trying to be overly critical... I just don't want to see this game become so narrative based that you lose diversity in character builds. Narrative Crunch Hybrid with a little more emphasis on narrative is awesome... but 80% narrative will push alot of fans away. In my opinion, 2nd Edition is something that would benefit from being something that pays a good amount of honor to the 1st edition but advances it to the more modern narrative approach that is popular at the moment. A blend of things for the old and new gamer.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: If ultimately the system has many optional rules that allow us to get something more akin to the 1-5 attrib and 1-5 skill then there really won't even be a problem. Any idea when we will get to see those optional rules? I'm also particularly interested in seeing how all things combat, damage, and armor works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-09-2017, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T19:16:10-07:00","id":1148489,"title":"","content":"I would presume that the limits are for mortal/heroic characters, and that there are additional points/dots/bonuses as one progresses to Demigod or God levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T20:24:40-07:00","id":1148506,"title":"","content":"Mental Force always struck me as being more about attention and recall than about reasoning and problem solving \u2014 for lack of a better term, Focus rather than Intellect. My preference would be to roll the reasoning and analysis stuff in with Mental Control, while Mental Force is more about how aware you are: I'd use it primarily for perception and recall: the ability to acquire the relevant facts for the situation at hand. Also, for the ability to process information: someone with high Mental Force should be able to sift through and organize mountains of information (the Mental equivalent of weight), whereas someone with high Mental <i>Control</i> should be adept at putting that information to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-09-2017, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T14:14:09-07:00","id":1149538,"title":"","content":"Favored approach seems to be creating additional complications to solve a non-problem. If the goal is to dissuade min-maxers you have failed to succeed. All it's done is limit character variety needlessly.<br /> <br /> For people saying faster NPC generation...who are you people? Every WW game I've played ever an NPC just has whatever stats I think they should have, and that's it. There is no formula, no math, no pools and no spending. How is this shorter than just a quick fiat?<br /> <br /> Also, I really hate they decided to go with Composure again for the Social Resistance trait name, but whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My preference would be to roll the reasoning and analysis stuff in with Mental Control, while Mental Force is more about how aware you are: I'd use it primarily for perception and recall: the ability to acquire the relevant facts for the situation at hand. </div> </div> </div>I wasn't sad to see Appearance dropped all those moons ago, but I do miss having a dedicated Perception attribute.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T11:33:47-07:00","id":1150182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1149538#post1149538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Favored approach seems to be creating additional complications to solve a non-problem. If the goal is to dissuade min-maxers you have failed to succeed. All it's done is limit character variety needlessly.<br /> <br /> For people saying faster NPC generation...who are you people? Every WW game I've played ever an NPC just has whatever stats I think they should have, and that's it. There is no formula, no math, no pools and no spending. How is this shorter than just a quick fiat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I don't like that it eliminates diversity. I don't need mechanics to disuade min-maxers... my group as a whole calls people out in min-maxing without justification all the time. Preventing min-maxing is a group problem to solve... not the systems.<br /> <br /> Regarding NPC generation... I basically said exactly what you did the first time I saw Chronicles of Darkness and it was a big reason why I switched very quickly from traditional d20. If a npc in a scene needs to do something I just think of what their attribute value for that action would be (1 = deficient, 2 = average, 3 = above average, 4 = Exceptional, 5 = pinnacle of man) then think of their skill level, (0 = untrained (add a penalty), 1 = novice, 2 = could make a living off of it, 3 = stands out among their professional peers, 4 = Outstanding skill, could likely lead entire teams, a company, or make developments in the field, and 5 = a god damn legend in the field that really leaves very little or nothing to criticize) then add 1-4 if needed based on additional skills/specialties/unique circumstances and apply any 9 or 8 again properties based on how routine the action would be for them. That forms the dice pool and then I roll it. Simple.<br /> <br /> The whole process takes no more than 5-10 seconds if you put even a mild amount of thought into the npc before the session or while the players are talking among themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-16-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T11:54:22-07:00","id":1150187,"title":"","content":"I don't think it feels like it harms character diversity. The system is the core of what makes it a game and the system is a contract between the players and the GM. If you have to depend on GM fiat to make your game function, it is probably a poor design. Further, this system feels like something inspired by Fate Core/Accelerated. I know we are all WoD/CofD fans, but this isn't the Storyteller system. Different games, with different use cases. New system makes sense, even if it pulls some verbiage from those more traditional systems. Maybe they could've branded their system differently to distinguish it from Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T12:30:30-07:00","id":1150191,"title":"","content":"Well, with the rules as written and that we know of it is impossible to make a guy with 4 Might 2 dex and 5 stamina. (EDIT ADD IN: Admittedly, this already required me to allow them to use power, finesse, and resistance as the 3 categories for attributes in CofD... but even something like that isn't present in StoryPath as we know it despite that house rule's popularity in storyteller.) A super tough and exceptionally strong guy who isnt deficient in dex but isn't great either. So mathematically it is already impossible to say it dones't reduce character diversity. With the system as is, id have to go with Physical 3 with a focus in resistance to even get close to what I wanted. That would give him 3 Might, 3 Dex, and 3 (+2 on rolls) stamina. Id have to then pick and choose among knacks or whatever else is available to try and make him stronger or seemingly stronger. That's more confusing then just giving me more control over my attributes. It's been mentioned that there is an option to make favored approach be a single attribute... but that doesnt fix that issue. Maybe if your favored approach was made up of any 3 attributes to more personalize your character but even that is needlessly limited and couldn't represent the character stat array above.<br /> <br /> As the system is, your attributes within each &quot;arena&quot; will all be the same base value before favored approach is applied. So we have people talking about what about the strong guy whos not smart... but what about the exceptionally manipulative person who has no social presence and otherwise wouldn't stand out at all? I really wish there is an optional rule to place points more freely and eliminate favored approach. I am really worried that favored approach will be referenced to by knacks, boons, and other aspects of the system and that it will be very difficult to phase out without rewriting alot of things... which would put us right back where we were with 1st edition in terms of adding additional work.<br /> <br /> Trust me, I get it. Storypath isn't storyteller. Onyx Path wants their own system to base games off and show their vision to the world. This is awesome. But my concern is that they are focusing too much on this painting characters in broad strokes approach due to the epic scale of the settings attached to the system. The negative to this approach is that mortal games are going to feel goofy. Mortals who are painted in broad strokes are likely going to feel uncomplex/bland and tropey which will reduce what you can do with the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm still holding hope that they don't want to limit diversity and that the information in the rest of origin and hero will allow you add the layer of diversity you need to separate characters but at the same time im nervous that with the delay we had already that the system is basically set in stone and may not have accounted for some things. There is plenty of time left though, Onyx Path will have plenty of time to create optional rules to help out players who don't want character creation to be painted with broad strokes but if favored approach is basically referenced everywhere in the first two books then im worried its going to be difficult to add in alternatives for people who don't like it without giving them a whole lot of homework. This is further frustrated by the fact they have been keeping system details so secretive since the delay.<br /> <br /> I just want a system that is going to be diverse and have lasting potential. I want to play Scion for ridiculous amounts of years in the future. I want to be able to tell intricate stories within all the tiers of the World. This isn't a post trying to complain to the devs and make em feel bad. This is more so a post of concern from a person who may be too big of a fan of Scion's setting for my own good.<br /> <br /> Even a minor post detailing some info into the design perspective that determined these mechanics would help get a grasp of things and sooth people's concerns I'm sure. If this is about them having serious passion for their vision of the game then I'm going to respect it alot more. We need to let Onyx Path embrace their proper vision of the game so that they have the passion to support it for the long haul. I wholeheartedly believe that. More transparency on the reasons behind their decisions to use these particular systems would go a long way. I feel confident that I can houserule the system enough that my group will love it, but what about the groups that don't have the experience with system editing that I do and never buy any additional books in the line? That's going to hurt the future of Scion.<br /> <br /> Hopefully this long post adequately describes my (and some other's) concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-16-2017, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T17:45:06-07:00","id":1150242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150191#post1150191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still holding hope that they don't want to limit diversity and that <b>the information in the rest of origin and hero will allow you add the layer of diversity you need to separate characters</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that already established?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1147570#post1147570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an optional rule in the SG chapter (one of many optional rules) that allows you to condense the Focus down to one Attribute if that's what you prefer - and yes, there are Conditions that come into play to emulate strong-but-stupid folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T20:33:20-07:00","id":1150260,"title":"","content":"Mostly, I have questions about skills.<br /> <br /> archery: it seems odd that bows use athletics instead of firearms. Sure, there is a component of physical strength, but thematically guns and bows are much more similar than lifting/running/jumping and bows. If Pilot governs submarine navigation and horseback riding, I feel firearms should govern guns and bows. Thrown weapons get a little trickier - tossing a boulder is a very athletic task, but throwing knives? not so much. Personally, I'd probably draw the line between blunt &amp; heavy (Athletics) and sharp &amp; light (firearms).<br /> <br /> Is the skill list complete? It seems unable to cover several significant tasks - arts, crafting, perception","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T21:18:14-07:00","id":1150266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150242#post1150242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that already established?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? Having to apply a permanent condition on your character to simply solve one problem such as dumb but strong isnt a solution to the inherant limiting aspects of character creation. Is there going to be a condition to emulate manipulative characters that have no presence other than dooming yourself to having 1 composure as well? In that example if you wanted to be thematically bad with social presence to symbolize that you are not notable socially or in a crowd but overall are playing a snake in the grass sort of character with high manipulation you would be forced to put one point into social, favored approach finesse, and be stuck with 1 composure. Generally speaking a snake in the grass master manipulator would be able to keep their cool... but ultimately the system as is wont let me do that. It also assumes that now that character is going to have a bare minimum of 3 dex (so there goes being able to make the character pudgy and clumsy in the physical department if I wanted to) and 3 cunning unless we use a optional rule which reduces your favored approach to a single attribute which I addressed above does not solve the inherant limiting factors.<br /> <br /> How about this... why don't you simply tell me what you personally like about this new approach compared to the 1-5 open approach that Scion 1st edition employed? Give me some perspective and perhaps you will convince me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"18839\" data-vbnamecard=\"18839\">zilaenor</a> - Honestly, Id be comfortable if they just put all ranged combat into a single skill since they put all melee into a single skill. The only thing missing on the list is craft and investigation but that seems to be an intentional omission considering they have more generalized rules for crafting and investigating which involve more than simply rolling some dice with some modifiers. (Which I do generally like. The crafting rules in particular seem pretty awesome.) Perception in Onyx Path style games is usually a mix of two attributes that you roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-17-2017, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T01:44:49-07:00","id":1150284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150266#post1150266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about this... why don't you simply tell me what you personally like about this new approach compared to the 1-5 open approach that Scion 1st edition employed? Give me some perspective and perhaps you will convince me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're judging, and asking others to judge, as system most of us have never actually played.<br /> <br /> And you basically already addressed this yourself in a previous post. Scion (and Trinity) are about larger than life characters where the diversity at character creation is less important. Your frustration seems born of the fact that this setup isn't as good for games that aren't the direct focus of the system.<br /> <br /> That's not a very convincing critique. &quot;This is fine for the intended feel of the default game, but not as good for using it for other things,&quot; doesn't really seem to justify all the worry over what seems to be the simplest house rule possible. If a starting character defaults to 1/2/3 in Arenas and +2 across a Focus, that's the same as each Attribute starting at 1, with 15 to assign as you desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:31:50-07:00","id":1150318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150266#post1150266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it? Having to apply a permanent condition on your character to simply solve one problem such as dumb but strong isnt a solution to the inherant limiting aspects of character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree and find that to be a completely valid solution.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:50:06-07:00","id":1150328,"title":"","content":"My gut on this says the base rules for char gen will either be put 1, 2, and 3 dots into each Arena and note your approach as power, finesse or resistance with the sidebar option being &quot;if you want to make each arena into three traits each you get x, y and z points to distribute over each arena in a priority order to raise stats from 1 before applying approach&quot; or just the inverse. In play this won't deeply matter since you'll be able to handle situations the same in system with either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:51:28-07:00","id":1150329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150284#post1150284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a starting character defaults to 1/2/3 in Arenas and +2 across a Focus, that's the same as each Attribute starting at 1, with 15 to assign as you desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it isnt. The sum of the number might be the same, but the array of possibilities is widely different.<br /> <br /> I made a fast math, and I got that the Storypath, in their Attributes only, have 18 possibilities. The Storyteller has 16200 different outcomes in attributes. Dis-considering the ones that let a character with a 1 in an attribute (for regular human sake) there are 324 different outcomes. (if I mathed wrong, please someone tell me in PM, and I edit here). The fact is, the Storypath system allow very little room for variation in the attributes part. But this is easily fixed without altering the Arena/Approach rules. If we have the option to start with maybe flaws or merits that affect specific attributes in a more roleplaying way (like a flaw that make your full dexterity only work out of combat, due to lack of training or something) then that wouldnt bother me so much.<br /> <br /> The situation I see here is that the game is made with a certain kind of character in mind, so the rules for attributes seem to be made to specifically accommodate that kind of character. That is not a problem, at least not in my eyes, as it allows a more focused gameplay that facilitates the game for that kind of character. We had the inverse problem in Scion 1ed, where a system for mortals tried to fit with Gods and Monsters, and became cumbersome. My problem with the actual attribute system is a simple one: why is the Approach/Arena rules are better for the Scion game?<br /> <br /> I dont see much advantage to compensate to the lack of freedom in the creation of the character. Maybe they decided that is the best way to interpret mythological beings, maybe they have the whole system build upon it and it worked so well that the lost of freedom on the attribute part seems worth it. As we dont know the whole game yet, I prefer to refrain myself from saying that it is a bad system, but I'm already thinking about how to house rule it. Hopefully the system will be great, with enough perks and different accessories to make each character unique and different, and all this house ruling wont be needed.<br /> <br /> Or they could explain to us why this attribute system choice instead of the regular Storyteller system. That would be very cool and would end this discussion, at least for me. But I trust they are trying what they believe to be the best for the game.<br /> <br /> About the rest of the system, I liked it. All seem very organic, very natural, but still better than Storyteller to tell a story. There is less focus on &quot;grit and dark reality&quot;, and more in the story telling aspect of a game that I like. The complications seem more natural to the character, the Compensation (or consolation, I dont remember now) is a great meta-idea for the game. The different levels for different characteristics of different beings is also a great idea, helping a lot to make a God fight in the same game as a Satyr. Even the little hinted about the damage in other updates seem surprisingly creative.<br /> <br /> I would be lying if I said I didnt like it very much, even if the Attribute section still bothers me, and I'm really expecting great things from this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T07:40:34-07:00","id":1150347,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I thought the point of seeing a system early was to get a feel for how it was going to be in the end and point out any potential flaws before they are made permanent? Your 15 point dispersed among the stats (with a cap of 5) was likely what I was going to go with for my houserule, yes. And then if any mechanics later on refer to your favored approach I would assume your 3 highest attributes (ties chosen by the player) would be considered your 3 favored attributes. Then if demigod and god raise things to 4 and 5 cap i'll simply make it raise things to a 6 and 7 cap. Same math.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar868_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"868\" data-vbnamecard=\"868\">danelsan</a> That only corrects a single character concept. I posted another example above which you didn't address.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12934_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12934\" data-vbnamecard=\"12934\">Manbat</a> Me and you are pretty close to being on the same exact page. If they have a intricate system of quirks and flaws that can shift attributes around or simulate such things then that would improve the system quite a bit... but ultimately it still has less diversity than the old system. I'm trying to be optimistic, im coming up with potential house rules like yourself, and simply wanting Neall to shed a little light onto why this system in particular is better for Scion 2nd ed. Good to see im not entirely crazy here in thinking this system makes me a bit nervous.<br /> <br /> Everything else in the Scion 2nd ed ruleset (cept maybe a couple of the skills that got blended together) is awesome. I love scale, I love the ability to portray mortals, mythical creatures, and godly beings all with the same system. I just don't want to see the system needlessly limit itself to being a broad stroke tropey setting that can only easily tell stories about characters who are not inherently complex. I love what they have told us about The World and I want to be able to tell all sorts of stories inside of it with many types of characters without having to houserule things excessively.<br /> <br /> More transparency would help tremendously. I'd love to hear Neall explain his passion for Scion 2nd ed and why he chose what he did and how it makes things better in his eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-17-2017, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T13:28:55-07:00","id":1150437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150329#post1150329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont see much advantage to compensate to the lack of freedom in the creation of the character. Maybe they decided that is the best way to interpret mythological beings...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is probably the biggest reason for it. In Scion 1e, many gods and even your own godly characters were put into a box by Fate. You had to follow fate meaning once you had a motif and a method, you had to follow it no matter what or risk fatebinding or causing complications to your character\u2019s identity. I think this is just a mechanical incentive to follow with that train of thought. Is your character a brawler? Very brash and direct like Thor? Maybe a future god of Pugilism? Great, you\u2019re always going to be direct because of Fate but you have a little room to work within that in social or mental tasks, but you can roleplay him as dumb or socially inept. I don\u2019t think the numbers on the page are going to entirely dictate the way you want to portray your character and Fate will have a lot of ways in which they are portrayed to the world and story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 10-18-2017, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T16:52:36-07:00","id":1150499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150329#post1150329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it isnt. The sum of the number might be the same, but the array of possibilities is widely different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is as close as needed for my point.<br /> <br /> As well, I don't find the array of possibilities to be an inherently good thing. I've been dealing with the ST family approach to this for over 20 years. I don't think that the nine Attributes are bad (like I don't want to see the collapse to 3 Attributes thing we've seen elsewhere), but the 7/5/3 spread (or whatever) having the ability to be spread in more ways hasn't struck me as something that's really added to the games over the years.<br /> <br /> Here's what all my experience has shown: ~95% of the time, players don't take advantage of the diversity possible for character reasons.<br /> <br /> Usually, players focusing on character end up with something pretty close to what Storypath generates. The default is towards the most even/general spread, with maybe one Attribute bumped up a bit. If I want to make an all-around athlete in the ST family systems, I can't dump stat any of the physical Attributes to be faithful to the concept. I might have one Attribute that gets a bigger part than others... but that's Storypath already<br /> <br /> I've seen way more characters with &quot;diverse&quot; spreads that were clearly picked because of system more than for character.<br /> <br /> I think that the diversity the old method allows is overrated. Simplification can go too far too, but it generally feels like the reasons given aren't really addressing the game design here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150347#post1150347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the point of seeing a system early was to get a feel for how it was going to be in the end and point out any potential flaws before they are made permanent?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's lots of reasons for previews. What you're talking about is open development. This wasn't released as such. This was released - as far as I can tell - because Scion 2e is behind schedule an Neall wanted to assure backers that progress is being made. Basically the point was, &quot;we delayed and core mechanics is a big reason why, here's the evidence we put work into that.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no call in the Kickstarter update for feedback on this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That only corrects a single character concept. I posted another example above which you didn't address. </div> </div> </div>Because the addressing of them isn't really needed. &quot;Conditions exist to help differentiate&quot; repeated ad nauseum doesn't add anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... but ultimately it still has less diversity than the old system. </div> </div> </div>Why, exactly, in the context of Scion, and the rest of the rules, is this actually a bad thing? You're posting as if maximum number of options is the best result. That assumption isn't one I think we all share. After all, 15 dots to spend where you want is more diverse than 7/5/3 that ST uses so often.. but people rarely complain that 7/5/3 is too restrictive as a default rule to ensure people spread out a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More transparency would help tremendously. I'd love to hear Neall explain his passion for Scion 2nd ed and why he chose what he did and how it makes things better in his eyes. </div> </div> </div>That isn't fair. Storypath isn't Neall's solo baby. Storypath is Onyx Path's in-house system and was group developed by multiple people at the company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T06:38:06-07:00","id":1150621,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I really don't feel like making a long post responding to everything you just said because I feel like we're just talking in circles about opinions. Long post short, I disagree with your view that it's not important because you haven't seen people use it to its fullest. I don't believe there is going to be an infinite amount of conditions to emulate every character concept. You don't think they should have to repeat &quot;a condition can fix that&quot; over and over yet you say this wasn't supposed to be judged because they didn't ask for feedback... Perhaps they didn't feel they needed to repeat that every post? I house ruled additional options of shifting points around in ST as well because I didn't think it was open enough... that should give you an idea of how I do things. And sure, StoryPath isn't Neall's baby... but story path started off as Scion's baby and Neall is Scion's new daddy... That and hes sort of the face as Scion at the moment. Is it really that odd id ask him primarily to respond? Hell, I'd take a response from anyone with answers at this point. I wasn't trying to put pressure on Neall or exclude others, I just want to know why this system is better enough to warrant change. I recently learned more about Trinity than I ever knew before and so my curiosity extends to wonder why it's better for Trinity as well. Both settings are very expansive and seem like they would benefit from a bit more detail in creation. Remember, these rules are being used for normal mortals as well...<br /> <br /> Overall, I don't think we are going to agree on this... And I don't think I'm going to get a response from anyone from Onyx Path. So I'm just going to do some minor prep work for possible house rules I could use (if the rest of the system doesn't pick up the slack) and just wait and see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T12:15:25-07:00","id":1150725,"title":"","content":"Me I'm going to wait until the full Chargen in the final version and the merits before I make a call on how viable various character builds are.<br /> <br /> Instead I'm going to focus on some other mechanics. Like I'm actually rather eager to test out this Social Persuasion System. Looks pretty elegant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:07:57-07:00","id":1150796,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Neill said there were alternate creation rules in the ST chapter. Until we see those as well I don't think it's fair to say whether character creation is good or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:19:55-07:00","id":1150803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150796#post1150796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, Neill said there were alternate creation rules in the ST chapter. Until we see those as well I don't think it's fair to say whether character creation is good or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's perfectly fair to comment on the rules we have been provided.<br /> <br /> All game design has one immutable trade-off: the benefit of the crunch versus the overhead of managing it. I've been playing Storyteller for forever, and managing its Attributes is really easy. Every time I teach it to people they pick it up by the 3rd session, tops. So, going to this version doesn't feel like it saves me much in the overhead department. On the other hand, it costs me a lot in terms of system diversity. Hell, if I have to pick up a mechanical widget (strong but dumb) on top the stats, instead of just using the stats themselves, I'm losing in the overhead department.<br /> <br /> Even if a character is &quot;larger than life&quot; that doesn't mean they fall neatly into one of about 18 character builds.<br /> <br /> Overall, I like the system as presented, but this Attribute system feels like unnecessary change for the sake of change. It kinda wants to be narrative, and kinda wants to be three-stat, yet wants to sell itself as nine stat.<br /> <br /> If there isn't an outta-the-box fix, it's going to take about five minutes for someone to bang one out. If the powers and such are tied into this little swamp, it's gonna kill my enthusiasm for anything else run on Storypath, including Aberrant, and that would be a damn shame. I've been waiting for 2E Aberrant for fifteen years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  typo. 10-18-2017, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:28:21-07:00","id":1150811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150803#post1150803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If there isn't an outta-the-box fix, it's going to take about five minutes for someone to bang one out. If the powers and such are tied into this little swamp, it's gonna kill my enthusiasm for anything else run on Storypath, including Aberrant, and that would be a damn shame. I've been waiting for 2E Aberrant for fifteen years.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there is an out of the box fix, or at least a couple optional ones. And the creation preview showed that even at character creation you can buy up individual attributes and even shuffle them around between sessions. So I think even without a RAW fix or houseruleing it would take maybe two sessions to fix the diversity issues. And none of the Knacks or Boons that have been spoiled even hint at being tied to arenas and favored approaches. I don't love the way you distribute starting stats either but I think there will be plenty of ways, both RAW and via houserule, to deal with it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:16:08-07:00","id":1150836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150621#post1150621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I really don't feel like making a long post responding to everything you just said because I feel like we're just talking in circles about opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but it does feel like you're dodging a question with all this: How much diversity here is enough? How many Attribute spreads do we need? 18 is too few... is 50 enough, is 500, does it need to be in the thousands? Why is this one of many traits in the system in need of all this diversity as well?<br /> <br /> Because part of the circling is around the assumption that, &quot;more diversity is better,&quot; not being examined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't believe there is going to be an infinite amount of conditions to emulate every character concept. </div> </div> </div>We don't need infinite conditions. We need a few pages of &quot;How to Make Conditions for [Storypath Game],&quot; so we can have the ones needed for the purpose they serve. I think the CofD would have benefited greatly from spending more time on building conditions instead of big lists of them and a few paragraphs on building new ones at the end of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't think they should have to repeat &quot;a condition can fix that&quot; over and over yet you say this wasn't supposed to be judged because they didn't ask for feedback... Perhaps they didn't feel they needed to repeat that every post? </div> </div> </div>These things are not related, nor is this an honest representation of what I said.<br /> <br /> I said that this preview wasn't posted as open development, so Neall isn't looking for feedback. I never said it wasn't &quot;supposed to be judged,&quot; even if I do thing there's a lot of judgement being made before all the details are out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And sure, StoryPath isn't Neall's baby... but story path started off as Scion's baby and Neall is Scion's new daddy... That and hes sort of the face as Scion at the moment. Is it really that odd id ask him primarily to respond? </div> </div> </div>This isn't accurate to my understanding of the history of Scion 2e, Storypath, and so on. It seems fairly clear that after Rich acquired Trinity and Scion for Onyx Path, that creating an in-house system for both was on the company's mind well before individual developers were assigned to each property. We've known that what would become Storypath has been coming for a very long time as something more than Scion 2e's system.<br /> <br /> And it's not odd to want to ask Neall things directly... we have a whole thread about it. Your phrasing that I responded to? That's pretty bad for getting developers to want to engage with you. Anyone that thinks - at this point in time - Neall needs to &quot;explain&quot; his passion for Scion isn't worth Neall's time to respond to. If I was Neall, or Ian, or just someone working for Onyx Path on any of the Storypath games, I wouldn't want to respond to you at this point, and I'd just wait for you to get the final product and with the knowledge that you're either going to let this one thing stick in your craw, or you're not, because game designers can't make everyone happy.<br /> <br /> You think more transparency would be better... but that's a fairly selfish view because you want someone to directly address your concerns. Watching the RPG industry in general says that, at this point in the process, transparency isn't an inherently good thing. The final product needs to be out for any productive official responses to occur. The Exalted 3e issues with exactly this sort of thing are plenty of evidence that having the developers responding to posters on the Internet did not make things better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Both settings are very expansive and seem like they would benefit from a bit more detail in creation. </div> </div> </div>If you have the full character creation rules to explain why you can accurately assert that the less options in Attribute assignments means character creation as a whole is not detailed enough, please do share.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, these rules are being used for normal mortals as well... </div> </div> </div>&quot;Normal&quot; as in, &quot;major characters in these games,&quot; not normal as, &quot;playing a slice of life genre high school game instead.&quot;<br /> <br /> Xander from Buffy: the Vampire Slayer is a normal human in the sense that Storypath wants to stat people. He's got no powers, no skill with magical arts, etc. I don't really see any issue with what we know of the Storypath system modelling him as a viable playable character or support NPC just because of the more limit method of generating Attributes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150803#post1150803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's perfectly fair to comment on the rules we have been provided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and it's also fair to call people out for comments that stretch too far from what we know to make assumptions about how the game with play once we have all the parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if a character is &quot;larger than life&quot; that doesn't mean they fall neatly into one of about 18 character builds. </div> </div> </div>18 Attribute assignment builds before customization points are applied. That's not counting all the differences in skills, Callings, Virtues, powers, etc.<br /> <br /> This is part of the problem with the doomsaying here about this one widget in the system. It's treating it as far more than one widget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:16:25-07:00","id":1150837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150811#post1150811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But there is an out of the box fix, or at least a couple optional ones. And the creation preview showed that even at character creation you can buy up individual attributes and even shuffle them around between sessions. So I think even without a RAW fix or houseruleing it would take maybe two sessions to fix the diversity issues. And none of the Knacks or Boons that have been spoiled even hint at being tied to arenas and favored approaches. I don't love the way you distribute starting stats either but I think there will be plenty of ways, both RAW and via houserule, to deal with it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really hear &quot;fix.' I heard &quot;take something that applies to three Attributes and apply it to one.&quot; Maybe I'm missing something; I only read the system once. That's doesn't sound like it gives me the versatility of the old system.<br /> <br /> I find the contention that the system won't matter two sessions in to be even more frustrating. Why am I pigeonholing my PCs for two frikking sessions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:09:01-07:00","id":1150850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150837#post1150837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't really hear &quot;fix.' I heard &quot;take something that applies to three Attributes and apply it to one.&quot; Maybe I'm missing something; I only read the system once. That's doesn't sound like it gives me the versatility of the old system.<br /> <br /> I find the contention that the system won't matter two sessions in to be even more frustrating. Why am I pigeonholing my PCs for two frikking sessions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then houserule it, it's the simplest houserule on the world. &quot;I'm giving you X points to put into attributes, have fun.&quot; Where x equals the total the RAW gives you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:49:54-07:00","id":1150865,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> <br /> I think enough people are agreeing with me here that I don't need to clarify any further. We will just have to see what Onyx Path decides to offer us in terms of options and ease of potential house ruling for this &quot;issue&quot; as many of us see it.<br /> <br /> I will answer your last questions, however. How much diversity is enough? Enough that my players can make whatever character they want or can think of with minimal need to make up new rules and conditions to break the almighty T spead the stats are going to look like. How will I likely solve this?<br /> <br /> 15 points wherever they want. Skills are no longer in categories so why should attributes? 1-5 range since its the same math with favored approach removed.<br /> <br /> What if favored approach is refrenced thruout the book? Il simply tally up all their stats in each of force, finesse, and resistance. Whichever is the highest is what their favored approach is considered but it has no mechanical benefit outside of being refrenced to. If a ability makes your favored approach +3 instead of +2 then il just give them +1 to those attributes or any 3 attributes of their choosing depending the frequncy of refrences to favored approach throughout the system.<br /> <br /> If hero, demigod, or god increases the stat cap higher then il simply add the increase to 5 instead of 3.<br /> <br /> Perhaps my history of the StoryPath system is off. Its very possible all things considered. As I said, my post was never to target or exclude any specific developers. This is the Scion section of the forums which i assumed is the section that mainly Neall pays attention to from the StortPath dev team... so I requested some of his insight into this particular complaint about the preview. I doubt Neall is disuaded by answering my question due to how I asked it. There was no disrespect pointed his way in how I phrased it. Many have asked the same question, so its not that i find myself so important that I need answered specifically. The point remains that several prople being concerned about the same thing in the past has invoked a reponse, and well... now we have several people.<br /> <br /> I think im good on continuing this conversatuon with you specifically though. We disagree, thats cool. I didnt make my post to end up spending hours going back and forth about it, (my mistake there... this is a forum afterall) I simply didn't want to let things go unmentioned and have it effect the longevity of StoryPath for alot of people.<br /> <br /> Hope we both enjoy the final product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-18-2017, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T03:40:30-07:00","id":1150945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150865#post1150865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think enough people are agreeing with me here that I don't need to clarify any further.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't follow. Since when was popularity the deciding factor in what is largely a two person conversation (also.. do you really want to get into counting such things if you want to bow out of this)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will answer your last questions, however. How much diversity is enough? </div> </div> </div>If you're actually going to, please do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Enough my players can make whatever they want,&quot; is not an answer, because there's no mechanical definition of those desires. If I want a character that's just the best at everything, should the system bend to let me have all the stuff at start? Or do we expect an arbitrary starting point that the designers try to make fit the expectations of their intended game play?<br /> <br /> Once you accept the arbitrary limits on character creation, what decides what's diverse enough? Even with 15 however I want, there's going to be concepts that don't fit. 15 however I want can also lead to extremely lopsided characters that might not mesh well with the intended game play. 15 is an arbitrary limit on maximum diversity as much as the Arena/Focus thing.<br /> <br /> So you're not answering the fundamental question: How much diversity does the game actually need in determining starting Attributes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Skills are no longer in categories so why should attributes? </div> </div> </div>Scion dropped Skills in categories in 1e. As well, it's something the ST family of games always put to a purpose. The WoD and CofD games use Skill groups to denote untrained penalties. Trinity grouped them by their most common linked Attribute to ease play. Exalted grouped them by character type affinity (even if this didn't always have a mechanical impact).<br /> <br /> Attributes should remain in categories as long as those categories serve a purpose. The 3 x 3 approach that the CofD adopted quickly proved to be a useful system widget, hence it's inclusion here. &quot;This power increases your character's height and mass to provide X Scale to Physical Arena actions,&quot; and, &quot;This potion of endurance gives a 2e enhancement to Resilience Approaches for the duration of its effects,&quot; are both clearly ways the Attribute categories are useful even if they're not useful for your char-gen preferences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was no disrespect pointed his way in how I phrased it. </div> </div> </div>Your intentions, what's actually in the text, and how others read it aren't all inherently the same thing. I certainly don't consider questioning Neall's passion for Scion respectful considering all the work he's done for it that shows he's exceedingly passionate about this project, and several people have liked my post where I pointed that out... so you know.... several people man.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:06:31-07:00","id":1150985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150850#post1150850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then houserule it, it's the simplest houserule on the world. &quot;I'm giving you X points to put into attributes, have fun.&quot; Where x equals the total the RAW gives you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the best you got is the classic Oberoni Fallacy? Try again.<br /> <br /> My critique centers on a very simple analysis: crunch must justify itself by providing some benefit to the players (in this case including the ST). The only benefit that has been described here for this system over the old one is it saves about 10 minutes during character creation. In exchange, the ability of people to make reasonable, diverse characters is greatly diminished.<br /> <br /> Waving a stick around and saying &quot;larger than life&quot; doesn't justify mechanical widgets to make strong and stupid, not when the older version has an easier way of doing so.<br /> <br /> So, I'm still waiting for someone to explain what I'm actually getting as a ST or a player in exchange for losing that diversity and simplicity at character creation. This isn't Shadowrun, or HERO, where character creation is a high barrier to entry.<br /> <br /> I'm not a grognard. I'd love a fresh, cool system that walks the line between narrative and crunch support. That's half the reason I backed the KS. But on this particular sub-system, I see a bunch of Capitalized Words that lampshade a less effective implementation of the ST system.<br /> <br /> So, if you have a rational analysis on what I gain by using this system other than the above, I'd love to hear it. Otherwise my critique stands, and based on this thread, I'm far from the only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:06:31-07:00","id":1150986,"title":"","content":"&lt; Sorry for double post. &gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  double post. 10-19-2017, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:36:15-07:00","id":1150996,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I think you misinterpreted me. The math I made before about the array of possibilities was considering the good old 7/5/3 distribution that has been with us since the dawn of the Storyteller system. I didnt even considered the 15 to all, cause I don't think it is a good system. I like the attributes are separated in categories, and I like that it helps you focus on the kind of the character you want. We wanting or not, RPG is still a game, and besides terms like &quot;Tanker&quot;, &quot;Support&quot; and &quot;DPS&quot; being mostly of MMO, it is still fairly useful to understand what is the focus of your character on the game, specially to combat, a topic that every player thinking about when building his/her character (even those who do not excel in the battlefield). I also like the Abilities are separated in categories, helps to guide the difficulties, and how do we build the tests.<br /> <br /> My problem with the system presented is more about the Approach than the Arena. I dont see why a Character, lets say a Archer, that should have a good Dexterity, should be also better than in Manipulation and Cunning. In this system, as far as I can see, if I want to do a Charming Dazzling Archer, that shoots arrows, sing songs, is fun to be about and has always friends, but in the hour of need he can hold his will and dont run from a fight (which I would consider that the best attributes would be Dexterity, Resolve and Charisma) I can't. If I can break the Arena to something more roleplay, or just give the option to create my Approach (choosing one attribute of each Arena), then for me the system is great.<br /> <br /> And, talking about the rest of the system, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>, I also really want to test the Persuasion system. I didnt get it very much, but I think it it is one of those things that I will only fully get when I actually try it. With the consolations and complications, did you also get a very &quot;TV series&quot; vibe from the system? Like, the characters, even when they fail, they get something, the story, sometimes, might get somewhat silly with the consolations (the own examples on the update are somewhat silly), and the Complications feel like a good way to create good between characters relations (the really good shooter, that doesnt like the smart-tech boy, need to work with him to help him shoot their way out because his hand was harmed by the villain (maybe a luck arrow shot, worth a momentum point) and he now cant shoot).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:47:07-07:00","id":1151001,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> Yea, I don't mind bowing out of something... and yea, a couple others agreeing was essentially what I was looking for when I made the post. I don't see the value in spending a good chunk of my time arguing back and forth (especially with someone who is constantly asking for a definitive numerical answer for a question there is no definitive numerical answer) over a tabletop system but I felt id be doing StoryPath in general a disservice if I didn't at least voice a concern about an issue that could hurt the longevity of the game. (And yes, I know you will likely want to attack me on the phrasing of that as well as if I think my opinion is all high and mighty or something) Perhaps I should have mentioned in my first post that this wasn't a post intended for back and forth discussion and more something to get the idea out there and being talked about, that's on me. There are some people who enjoy doing these back and forths with people and now that likely a couple of them have chimed in to agree with the concept I figure they can continue from here. They enjoy it, I don't.<br /> <br /> It also comes down to the fact that I don't think your style of back and forth is beneficial. You seem to simply want to attack any random weak points u see in the post as a whole regardless if it has much weight to the overall discussion or not. This is frustrating to defend against. So I'd rather not do it. I only responded this time to address my next point.<br /> <br /> At what point in time did I ever question Neall's passion for the game? I mentioned Neall's passion because I truly believe he has a shit ton of it for Scion. This is an example of you wanting to attack any point that seems remotely weak in my post. I reference to Neall's passion about Scion 2nd ed (which i believe is very real and basically the core reason I even gave a shit about a 2nd edition being in the works after I listened to and read his interviews.) and you automatically take it as me questioning his passion rather than respecting it. I wanted Neall's opinion regarding the change because I was legitimately intrigued/concerned/confused as to why they decided to change such a fundamentally functional and tested system for one that seemed more restrictive after a couple of reads. Let's be honest, the preview was sold as a the FULL system but it entirely excluded combat, armor, health, healing, and now apparently conditions to modify attributes builds which was only brought up after we began this discussion. I get that some of that will be setting specific and can be argued to not need to be in a pure Story Path preview but considering that it was already stated that part of the rules adopted by Scion from the Trinity Team's work was a system regarding damage and armor... it seems odd to exclude it.<br /> <br /> So lets see if we can answer this question you want a definitive answer to. It's not definitive. Its a feeling of enough freedom that you don't feel like you are playing a minigame to assign your points. The amount of points given is an agreed upon powerscale in which we essentially agree is good for describing a starting character. I don't need to worry about people taking the 15 points anywhere rule and making some unrealistically lop sided characters because I trust my group and they all call bullshit on unproportional characters. So for my group, 15 anywhere is going to be a great solution. One of them may randomly make a bone head with massively inflated Physical Stats and garbage everything else but ultimately that will create an interesting story. A character with such low intelligence and social understanding is likely going to end up becoming more and more destructive and uncomfortable to be around the more power he gets and the more is expected of him that he can't comprehend because hes all muscle and zero brains/tact. So yea, lopsided character who likely will create some interesting rp. I don't like the feeling that my players need to come to me to house rule together conditions to properly portray their characters. Id rather focus that collaborative time on coming up with custom relics or boons they want to use to express their characters. I don't think a system should encourage the players to need the ST to create a personalized character (cept in some really cool edge cases which I think relics and boons qualify.)<br /> <br /> You mention that even with 15 points there are some concepts you can't do. True. But it is atleast enough points to make basically any believable mortal that isn't batman tier. Enough for my group to make whatever they want is a legitament answer for my group. I trust my group to realize that if they need more than 15 points then they are likely trying to describe a more advanced character and they could probably lose a couple points here or there. For example, my big oaf all physical guy above. There was a time where he was a slightly less muscular but still oafy individual. Go back to that point and make that the time he meets up with the rest of the group or gets his visitation. If everyone at the table needs more than 15 points then I'll consider making the campaign begin at a higher XP amount than normal. This is what frustrates me with arguing back and forth with your particular style of debating. You want me to explain in great detail all these fringe cases that avoid the core issue I even proposed to begin with. You can't make a pudgy snake in the grass character with low presence, high manipulation, above average composure, and low dex due to physical clumsyness. That's a fact. Do the math. Despite the fact that it is a legitament character concept and something that would be easy to do without ST help in many of the precusor systems that have led to StoryPath we now need to work together to create conditions to make him clumsy because his dex automatically needs to be high because his manipulation is high. Now this leads into you likely mentioning that you can shift points around after sessions and can increase particular stats as you gain xp so why does starting attributes matter so much... it matters because why should my players need to do a song and dance to get their stats where they want them to be overtime (even when their concept works easily with 15 points) when they could have had them from the start and been able to get started on portraying their character properly rather than portraying their change to proper representation over the first couple sessions?<br /> <br /> How I would deal with someone who needs more than 15 points is completely moot and only serves to bloat my response posts. About the only benefit of me discussing things such a level of detail is if someone reading this is trying to decide how he wants to handle things and appreciates the tips. If there is, awesome. The point remains that StoryPath doesn't even address the what if they need more than 15 points so why should my house ruling have to address it? Busy work. Strawman targets. No system is entirely perfect for everyone.<br /> <br /> My statement of why should attributes be locked to categories if skills are not was more or less just an observation that supported it wouldn't be a big deal to let people have complete control of their attribute system placement since skills are not like that. This likely stems from the fact that CofD is the core system I am used to using so my mind relates things to that subconsciously. I agree that categories have a place in the game and your examples of adding scale to physical or resistance are good examples. This however does not justify attributes needing to conform around them so strictly during character creation.<br /> <br /> If you have any issues with my particular ideas I have posted above then feel free to give me constructive criticism on them. If you want me to explain fringe cases that likely depend on individual ST preferences, common sense, or a &quot;we will see as we go&quot; type approach then I'm likely no longer going to respond to it. That's the part of debating with you that isn't fun. If you are legitimately interested in my opinions on those matters then that is a different story... it just seems you are trying to give me busy work rather than focusing on the original point.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Your criticism that my txt regarding Neall seemed like I was questioning his passion is reasonable considering multiple people have gotten that from it. This was not my intent, and apologize if it came off that way. I respect Neall greatly as a dev and simply would have respected greatly his opinion on this mechanic. My view on it was that he is more passionate about this project than most if not all of us and if he thinks it is a good choice then I'd like to know why. You likely are wondering why I'd even question it if I wasn't intending to question his passion. I'm simply not the type of person to hold someone on a pedestal of perfection. I can't see any benefit to the system at the moment. That's enough motivation to ask questions despite my faith in Neall's vision for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-19-2017, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T11:11:37-07:00","id":1151073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150985#post1150985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the best you got is the classic Oberoni Fallacy? Try again.<br /> <br /> My critique centers on a very simple analysis: crunch must justify itself by providing some benefit to the players (in this case including the ST). The only benefit that has been described here for this system over the old one is it saves about 10 minutes during character creation. In exchange, the ability of people to make reasonable, diverse characters is greatly diminished.<br /> <br /> Waving a stick around and saying &quot;larger than life&quot; doesn't justify mechanical widgets to make strong and stupid, not when the older version has an easier way of doing so.<br /> <br /> So, I'm still waiting for someone to explain what I'm actually getting as a ST or a player in exchange for losing that diversity and simplicity at character creation. This isn't Shadowrun, or HERO, where character creation is a high barrier to entry.<br /> <br /> I'm not a grognard. I'd love a fresh, cool system that walks the line between narrative and crunch support. That's half the reason I backed the KS. But on this particular sub-system, I see a bunch of Capitalized Words that lampshade a less effective implementation of the ST system.<br /> <br /> So, if you have a rational analysis on what I gain by using this system other than the above, I'd love to hear it. Otherwise my critique stands, and based on this thread, I'm far from the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already admitted I'm not a fan of the stat assignment presented in the preview. That's not what I'm debating. I'm debating that untill we see what modular options are offered we should withhold final judgment. I've seem a lot of systems that present the &quot;noob friendly&quot; as the default and give the better rules as options for people that are more comfortable thinking of concepts that need more flexibility. The added incredible ease of house rules seems to make this a relitive non-issue. Ok It's a flaw in the bog standard set-up., but there are multiple ways around it. I think we both agree it's a problem, I just see it as less of one than you do. So truce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T12:10:35-07:00","id":1151085,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12934_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12934\" data-vbnamecard=\"12934\">Manbat</a> - The Consolation and Complications do seem to have a TV Show type thing, but it also seems to fall into a growing sentiment in tabletop games that I've seen. The Fail Forward philosophy.<br /> <br /> Because there's not much that's fun about going &quot;Well you didn't succeed at the roll, so... Um... Er... I was kind of hoping you would, but you don't find any leads&quot;. So let's change the mindset, make it so even a failure helps move the story along.<br /> <br /> ... It also reminds me somewhat of something that someone said about Contrivances in movies. You can have one or two Contrived Moments in a movie to help the plot, but they need to have Complications attached. The example I saw specifically was for Who Framed Roger Rabbit?<br /> <br /> Eddie's hit a dead end in his investigation, and he and Roger duck into a theater. It just so happens that a newsreel gives him a clue as to what's going on. That's the Contrivance.<br /> <br /> But it just so happens that the lead he got? It leads him to <b>Toon Town</b>, where Eddie does <i>not</i> want to go. That's the Complication.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I like the Consolation and Complications. Failures turn into opportunities, and above all else, <i>keep the story moving</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T17:27:26-07:00","id":1151162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1150996#post1150996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you misinterpreted me. The math I made before about the array of possibilities was considering the good old 7/5/3 distribution that has been with us since the dawn of the Storyteller system.</div> </div> </div> </div>My response to you was under that assumption. Though the same question posed remains: how much diversity in Attribute assignments do we need? Pointing out that one option has X, and one option has Y never addresses if there's value in having that many.<br /> <br /> For example it's easy for modern car manufacturers to make cars that can go 150+ mph, and customers generally associate speed with quality. But why don't most cars go that fast? Because that speed comes with increased price, and most people never get to drive that fast. Most people aren't going to pay 10%-25% more for a model that goes faster when they never drive that fast. That extra speed sounds good, but it lacks practical value.<br /> <br /> IMO, the focus on Attribute assignment in this thread is in the same place. The diversity available was higher than most people used, so it had no practical value. Obviously you disagree, but you're never setting a goal post for the &quot;right&quot; amount of diversity to discuss. As much as someone else expressed they felt this feels like change for the sake of change, what if the negative reactions are just the opposite thereof?<br /> <br /> A lot of the rest of what you seem to think I was interpreting as you, were responses to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9236\" data-vbnamecard=\"9236\">Yig1015w</a> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My problem with the system presented is more about the Approach than the Arena. I dont see why a Character, lets say a Archer, that should have a good Dexterity, should be also better than in Manipulation and Cunning. </div> </div> </div>But &quot;Archer&quot; isn't a concept dictated by Attributes. There isn't an &quot;archery&quot; Attribute. Archery is covered by the Athletics Skill. A Dexterity 1/Athletics 5 character with a 1e finely tuned box is still looking at an average of 3 successes... which is pretty good. While it's hard to say how much remains, from previous previews we say things like combat Attributes not being static. Ranged weapons aren't always Dexterity, so an archer may or may not want to favor Dexterity depending on how they approach their attacks.<br /> <br /> Hercules was a renowned archer, but nobody would assign him an Approach of Finesse, but Dexterity 3/Athletics 5 plus powers is already a really good archer. But he generally wasn't portrayed as a Robin Hood/Errol Flynn archer (for whom high levels of Manipulation and Cunning make perfect sense), but something that would make perfect since with an Intellect (since Force is definitely Hercules' Approach): with single well placed shots from a bow strong for his massive strength with deliberate effect (earlier previews suggested that longer range/sniping ranged attacks use Intellect as the suggested Attribute).<br /> <br /> The Attributes are broad, and it seems like a lot of the worries are based on assumptions not in either this preview or older ones. &quot;I need high Dexterity to be a good archer,&quot; isn't necessarily something the system actually uses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1151001#post1151001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I don't mind bowing out of something... and yea, a couple others agreeing was essentially what I was looking for when I made the post.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... then can you reconsider the rather large number of moments in your post where you aim things at me as a person? You wanted to post something and have it validated... it's not my fault that when I tried to engage you in a discussion of your post you didn't want a discussion, but opted to engage anyway. That's your choice. It's not my posting style, or how I &quot;make things unfun,&quot; for you, or your repeated assertions of things I didn't say, or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (especially with someone who is constantly asking for a definitive numerical answer for a question there is no definitive numerical answer) </div> </div> </div>... but that' my whole point!<br /> <br /> People are complaining about reduction in the numerical diversity of Attribute selection in character creation, but refusing to actually discuss the numerical impacts of that line of thinking.<br /> <br /> If you think there isn't a definitive numerical answer, than &quot;this has less potential options than this other method,&quot; is not a logically valid critique. There needs to be a numerical answer if the complaint is numerical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> over a tabletop system but I felt id be doing StoryPath in general a disservice if I didn't at least voice a concern about an issue that could hurt the longevity of the game. (And yes, I know you will likely want to attack me on the phrasing of that as well as if I think my opinion is all high and mighty or something) </div> </div> </div>I never attacked you personally about that. I have called this doomsaying... because I think it's doomsaying.<br /> <br /> The longest running RPG in history is D&amp;D.. clearly Ability/Attribute diversity isn't the lynch-pin of longevity. Lots of games with widely panned mechanics have extremely long legs in terms of people actually playing them. Saying an Attribute selection process you think is too restrictive is actively detrimental to the health of the game is hyperbolic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At what point in time did I ever question Neall's passion for the game? </div> </div> </div>I appreciate your edit at the bottom of this, but I'm going to address this directly, because these are your words:<br /> <br /> &quot;I'd love to hear Neall explain his passion for Scion 2nd ed and why he chose what he did and how it makes things better in his eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your phrasing is, &quot;Neall explain his passion for Scion 2nd ed.&quot; I understand your clarified intent, but not just other people reading things like I did, can you not see how this phrasing is a problem? The way you wrote it, it isn't, &quot;why is Neall who's so passionate about this convinced this is good for the game?&quot; but, &quot;Neall needs to explain how he's passionate about the game and why this is good for the game.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's OK. We make mistakes, and you've clarified this point. But this is why I said that intent, words, and interpretations don't inherently line up. I completely believe you did not intend to question Neall's passion, but your wording did. I don't care how many people agree with me, or you, or whatever. I called your phrasing out because I felt it should be.<br /> <br /> But you're attacking me directly in saying that I'm not trying to discuss in good faith, because of your poor phrasing... and you're blaming me for making things unfun. That's not OK.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be honest, the preview was sold as a the FULL system... </div> </div> </div>No, it wasn't. The preview literally says &quot;core system&quot; three times. Core system is not the whole system with all the other details you bring up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its a feeling of enough freedom that you don't feel like you are playing a minigame to assign your points. </div> </div> </div>OK, so what &quot;feels&quot; like a minigame?<br /> <br /> To my understanding, when talking about games, minigames are when something has enough detail and options that it could be it's own game outright. That is, something is a minigame when it has enough moving parts to be a game.<br /> <br /> To me, that says you want less options, not more. Four decisions (rank Arenas from 1 to 3, pick a favored Approach) is less of a minigame, because it's fast and there's not a lot of gaming to do. A pool of 15 is far more the minigame, because now I have 15 decisions to make, and there's more to correlate to the rest of the system. &quot;I want to focus on social stuff, but I don't want to be a burden in combat, so how much can I pull from Physical to Social Attributes?&quot; is something I might consider with the straight 15 pool. That feels like a minigame to me.<br /> <br /> You don't have to play that minigame and can just assign the dots where you feel eyeballs the best... but you can do the same with Arenas/Focus.<br /> <br /> So this doesn't seem to work as an answer. Even getting away from purely numerical issues, you're talking about a &quot;feel&quot; but not relating it to the mechanics that communicate that feeling. If I want to avoid minigames and likely decision paralysis when making a game, I want to reduce options/diversity, not increase them. So... how is the Storypath method not better for getting rid of minigaming Attribute selection?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't need to worry about people taking the 15 points anywhere rule and making some unrealistically lop sided characters because I trust my group and they all call bullshit on unproportional characters. </div> </div> </div>That's you and your group. Scion is being made for a much larger group of people. It's not a fair criticism of the game to say that you'd prefer a different method despite a clear problem with it, because that problem isn't one your group would personally face. From a general design perspective, it's always better to have rules that people can change, than have no rules and force people to make up their own (which is not the same as rules where there's an inherent player creativity aspect, in Mage players make up their own spells, but that's not no rules because there's all the rules for building custom spells).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't make a pudgy snake in the grass character with low presence, high manipulation, above average composure, and low dex due to physical clumsyness. </div> </div> </div>Well, you can't with just Attributes, but you're also purposefully adding aspects of fulfilling a concept beyond what Attributes cover.<br /> <br /> To the base concept of &quot;Snake in the Grass master manipulator,&quot; Social Arena 3/Focus Finesse makes perfect sense. You're not a snake in the grass with low Presence. You need Presence to do things that hide that you're a snake. Low Presence/high Manipulation is Grima Wormtongue (you know, the guy that's known to be a manipulator even if he's good at it hence the moniker), where good Presence/high Manpulation is a character more like Littlefinger where lots of people trust you because you're good as doing things via Presence as well as Manipulation as needed. The idea that you should reduce Presence in Storypath's definitions thereof doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> &quot;Pudgy&quot; and &quot;Clumsy&quot; are additional details beyond the core character. Pudgy is just a descriptor of looks. A pudgy guy could just be out of shape, or could be a purposefully disguised martial arts master with insane physical traits. Dexterity is broader than if you are clumsy or not. And these edge case descriptors if meant to be mechanically significant is why the game has Conditions as has been addressed. This is a big problem with your examples. You're citing subsections of what Attributes do as reasons to reduce them. &quot;I want my character to be clumsy, so they can't have Dexterity 3+,&quot; is not engaging with the definition of Dexterity provided.<br /> <br /> There's also Skills. A Physical Arena 1/Finesse Focus character with that Dexterity 3 plays a lot different depending on their Skills. No Skill dots in things like Athletics, and Technology are going to make for quite the klutz.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can construct examples that don't fit well if you keep trying at it... but that's essentially no different than me trying to make a character than &quot;needs&quot; 17 dots instead of 15. You've already acknowledged that there's a need to compromise on these things, and players need to make characters that fit within the guidelines provided instead of trying to make ones that don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T08:09:23-07:00","id":1151327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1147432-storypath-system-preview?p=1151073#post1151073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already admitted I'm not a fan of the stat assignment presented in the preview. That's not what I'm debating. I'm debating that untill we see what modular options are offered we should withhold final judgment. I've seem a lot of systems that present the &quot;noob friendly&quot; as the default and give the better rules as options for people that are more comfortable thinking of concepts that need more flexibility. The added incredible ease of house rules seems to make this a relitive non-issue. Ok It's a flaw in the bog standard set-up., but there are multiple ways around it. I think we both agree it's a problem, I just see it as less of one than you do. So truce?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, truce.<br /> <br /> Consider all my statements prepended with &quot;From what we have here.&quot; I'm always willing to revise my thoughts as more information becomes available. They sent out the &quot;full core system,&quot; so it seemed like a good time to say stuff.<br /> <br /> So now it's time to talk about other things or wait until we have more info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:18:39-07:00","id":1151352,"title":"","content":"It's funny. I see a lot of debate over the degree of flexibility presented in the core system preview, over how much or how little you can do with nine different stats. I play GURPS, which only has four stats, and with the assorted skills, advantages, disadvantages, and optional rules, you can do pretty much anything - I doubt that nine is going to be a barrier to creativity. The new system is supposed to cover everything from humans to sun gods, and all the degrees in between, and apparently playtesting says it works. If all you have is the preview, I would suggest withholding judgement until the full end product is available, and you can see exactly what the options and plug-ins are. Right now, you'really arguing over the final performance of a car when you only have the engine in your hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}